      "lastReply": "A young tiger named Raja lived deep in the jungle, where he spent his days hunting and roaming. One evening, he caught the scent of something incredible drifting through the trees — fragrant rice, warm spices, and tender meat. Following his nose, he found a small dhaba at the forest's edge, where the cook was preparing biryani. Raja watched from the shadows, mesmerised by the careful layering of rice and the way the steam rose from the pot.\n\nThe next day, Raja returned and shyly asked the cook to teach him. The cook laughed at first, but seeing the tiger's earnest eyes, he agreed. Raja learned to soak the rice, roast the spices, and marinate the meat with yoghurt and ginger. His paws were clumsy at first, but he practised every night, adjusting the heat and tasting carefully until the flavours sang.\n\nWord spread through the jungle, and soon animals gathered at Raja's den every Friday evening. The tiger who once hunted alone now served steaming plates of biryani to deer, monkeys, and even a nervous rabbit. Raja had found something better than any hunt — the joy of sharing a meal he made with his own paws.\n\n6:18 PM",
